t flexible I'm I'm really  flexible little did I know that  disability was in fact the tower that  had changed my life completely I'm Troy  James and I'm a creature actor I play  creatures on TV and movies that move in  ways that make the audience squirt my  talent is the bat all of my joints my  legs my arms my shoulders my fingers  they just bend over I want them to so if  you need an alien demon or a nonhuman  creature that doesn't move in ways that  normal human people do that's when you  call me it looks like what I do is  extremely painful really it doesn't hurt  at all I don't know why I am as flexible  as I am  it's just something I was born with I'm  the only one of my family who can bed  dis arms and legs the way I do I didn't  think it was that strange until other  kids told me it was but they weren't  very nice about it and I remember being  very embarrassed and I hid it away  because what makes you different when  you're growing up isn't something to be  proud of I hid it for a long time but  that all changed when I caught a job as  an amusement park ride operator there's  a hot day the ride was down for some  reason or another the guests were  getting kind of ornery and I thought why  don't I show them what I could do and I  went up and down the line making really  cool shapes with my body and it was a  hit and that was the first time I gotten  that sort of positive reaction from  other people showcasing my talent I  never thought my ability was anything  more than a really cool party trick my  friend put his camera up to me and said  show me something cool then he posted it  on the Internet  and all of a sudden my phone started  ringing I started getting calls to be  cast in TV shows and I didn't look back  if you had told me a year ago I was  going to be an actor I would have  laughed at you but after some of my  performances people have told me that  it's not just the way I'm with my body  that's effective it's the acting behind  it I bring a reacti